"Benjamin A. Schmit" <benjamin.schmit@gmail.com> writes:

> Generally, the earlier the first wish, the more likely a death
> afterwards.

This is obviously true as the later the wish, the more games in which
you have already died are not being counted. On the other hand, I would
say, the earlier the wish, the larger the jump in probability to ascend.

> So let's assume an extremely benevolent RNG and go all the way back to
> the starting room.  Basically, I'd go for either good armour or a good
> weapon.

I don't think you should wish for a weapon first. Mostly because it will
only kill monsters. To win the game, however, you need to *survive*. And
most of the interesting weapons do double damage, so they are less
optimal when not fully enhanced.

> Which might well mean that I'll fall to poison (a spiked pit
> or an early poisonous monster). 

I think the poisonous monster thing can be ruled out pretty much thanks
to Elbereth and MC.

> Since poison is a relatively common early cause of death (before
> acquiring the resistance in some way), that'd be YASD, according to
> the theory.

Would it? Or rather a sign of not taking the necessary precautions? Like
going into the Mines, or not watching enough where you move.

